{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MoXQUqhGnmDEG1c7MNEp5H","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Acceptance Criteria: Track LLM token usage and runtime metrics\n2\t\n3\t**Issue:** QuantAgent-69d  \n4\t**Related:** [RQ](../01_requirements/QuantAgent-69d-RQ-token-time-metrics.md) | [DS](../03_design/QuantAgent-69d-DS-token-time-metrics.md)\n5\t\n6\t## AC-1: Successful call persists telemetry\n7\t**Given** an instrumented LLM call completes successfully  \n8\t**When** the call returns  \n9\t**Then** one `logs` row with `event_type = \"llm_call\"` exists  \n10\t**And** it contains `duration_ms > 0`  \n11\t**And** includes `provider`, `model`, and `operation` in structured fields/metadata\n12\t\n13\t## AC-2: Token fields are nullable by provider capability\n14\t**Given** a provider response does not expose token usage  \n15\t**When** the telemetry row is persisted  \n16\t**Then** token fields are null  \n17\t**And** `duration_ms` plus execution context are still present\n18\t\n19\t## AC-3: Failed calls still produce evidence\n20\t**Given** an instrumented LLM call raises an exception  \n21\t**When** QuantAgent records the failure  \n22\t**Then** one `logs` row with `event_type = \"llm_call\"` still exists  \n23\t**And** the structured metadata marks the status as error  \n24\t**And** `duration_ms > 0`\n25\t\n26\t## AC-4: Backtest aggregation stays isolated\n27\t**Given** backtest run A and backtest run B both generate LLM calls  \n28\t**When** metrics are queried for backtest run A  \n29\t**Then** the aggregate excludes rows from backtest run B\n30\t\n31\t## AC-5: Session aggregation stays isolated\n32\t**Given** two executions use different `thread_id` values  \n33\t**When** metrics are queried for one `thread_id`  \n34\t**Then** only rows for that `thread_id` are included\n35\t\n36\t## AC-6: Aggregate output is decision-useful\n37\t**Given** at least one stored telemetry row for a session or backtest  \n38\t**When** the aggregate query runs  \n39\t**Then** it returns call count  \n40\t**And** token sums  \n41\t**And** duration sum and average  \n42\t**And** a per-`operation` breakdown\n43\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6027cba3-e69d-464f-aa78-e9e9792aa2ae","uuid":"c9edffc7-913e-4e19-afc9-25fb03996985","timestamp":"2026-05-12T17:59:08.741Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/autodev-worktrees/QuantAgent/QuantAgent-69d/planner-20260512T124234Z/docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-69d-AC-token-time-metrics.md","content":"# Acceptance Criteria: Track LLM token usage and runtime metrics\n\n**Issue:** QuantAgent-69d  \n**Related:** [RQ](../01_requirements/QuantAgent-69d-RQ-token-time-metrics.md) | [DS](../03_design/QuantAgent-69d-DS-token-time-metrics.md)\n\n## AC-1: Successful call persists telemetry\n**Given** an instrumented LLM call completes successfully  \n**When** the call returns  \n**Then** one `logs` row with `event_type = \"llm_call\"` exists  \n**And** it contains `duration_ms > 0`  \n**And** includes `provider`, `model`, and `operation` in structured fields/metadata\n\n## AC-2: Token fields are nullable by provider capability\n**Given** a provider response does not expose token usage  \n**When** the telemetry row is persisted  \n**Then** token fields are null  \n**And** `duration_ms` plus execution context are still present\n\n## AC-3: Failed calls still produce evidence\n**Given** an instrumented LLM call raises an exception  \n**When** QuantAgent records the failure  \n**Then** one `logs` row with `event_type = \"llm_call\"` still exists  \n**And** the structured metadata marks the status as error  \n**And** `duration_ms > 0`\n\n## AC-4: Backtest aggregation stays isolated\n**Given** backtest run A and backtest run B both generate LLM calls  \n**When** metrics are queried for backtest run A  \n**Then** the aggregate excludes rows from backtest run B\n\n## AC-5: Session aggregation stays isolated\n**Given** two executions use different `thread_id` values  \n**When** metrics are queried for one `thread_id`  \n**Then** only rows for that `thread_id` are included\n\n## AC-6: Aggregate output is decision-useful\n**Given** at least one stored telemetry row for a session or backtest  \n**When** the aggregate query runs  \n**Then** it returns call count  \n**And** token sums  \n**And** duration sum and average  \n**And** a per-`operation` breakdown\n","numLines":43,"startLine":1,"totalLines":43}}}
