{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01NGCVK3qnDBzWf9xttsUib8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have everything I need. Let me write the test file for `llm_telemetry.py`. Let me set up a todo list and start writing the tests.\n\nThe key things to test based on the AC docs:\n1. AC-1: Successful call persists telemetry with duration_ms > 0 and context fields\n2. AC-2: Token fields nullable when provider doesn't expose usage\n3. AC-3: Failed calls still produce a log row with status=error\n4. AC-4: Backtest aggregation stays isolated\n5. AC-5: Session aggregation stays isolated\n6. AC-6: Aggregate output has call count, token sums, duration sum/avg, by_operation\n\n\n7. Unit tests for `extract_usage()` with different response shapes, `_aggregate_rows()` edge cases, `TelemetryCtx` dataclass defaults, and `invoke_with_retry` with telemetry context\n\nFor `persist_llm_call`, I need to handle the database mocking since it creates its own `SessionLocal()` session. I should check if the existing conftest has a `db_session` fixture I can leverage for testing.\n\nSince `persist_llm_call` doesn't accept a db parameter but the aggregation functions like `get_session_metrics` and `get_backtest_metrics` do, I'll mock `SessionLocal` to return my test session for the former, while using the fixture directly for the latter.\n\nWriting the test file...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2466,"cache_read_input_tokens":57163,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2466},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6027cba3-e69d-464f-aa78-e9e9792aa2ae","uuid":"0a71975b-ef5c-4a23-b7c1-6fb3694bea86"}
